sentences.l:
Indeed he was about to take up the fine goblet,
golden, two-eared, and was even then turning it in his hands,
that he might drink of the wine;

sentences.t:
τίς κ’ οἴοιτο μετ’ ἀνδράσι δαιτυμόνεσσι
μοῦνον ἐνὶ πλεόνεσσι, καὶ εἰ μάλα καρτερὸς εἴη,
οἷ τεύξειν θάνατόν τε κακὸν καὶ κῆρα μέλαιναν;

sentences.tr:
tis k’ oioito met’ andrasi daitymonessi
mounon eni pleonessi, kai ei mala karteros eiē,
hoi teuxein thanaton te kakon kai kēra melainan;

sentences.l:
He bent over to the other side, and the cup fell from his hand
as he was struck, and at once a spout, thick, up through the nostrils came
of human blood;

for this man urged on these deeds,
not so much needing marriage nor desiring it,
but thinking other things, which for him did not fulfil the son of Cronus,

and upon him let us all hold on,
massed together, if we may thrust him from the threshold and the doors,
and let us go up through the town, and let a shout most swiftly arise;

So then having spoken he drew the sharp sword,
bronze, on both sides pointed, and leapt at him,
frightfully shouting;

and at the same moment heavenly Odysseus
sent off an arrow, and struck the chest beside the breast,
and in his liver fixed the swift shaft;

and he struck the earth with his forehead,
in his heart distressed, and with both feet the chair
kicking he shook;

but then him anticipated
Telemachus, from behind having struck him with a bronze-fitted spear
between the shoulders, and through the chest he drove it;
